{"step_index":90,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:52:54Z","input_tokens":2774,"cache_read_tokens":139229,"output_tokens":2234,"thinking":"The `sfx` process completed its initial deliverables just before the server restart, as indicated by the timestamps on files related to audio processing. This suggests that the restart might be related to the completion of this task.\n\n\nThe restart interrupted several processes in various states. The `sfx` process completed before the restart. The `env-2` agent was building assets and updating scripts when it was interrupted. The `anim` agent completed several script updates and was waiting on another process when the server restarted. The `monitor` agent requires a specific command to resume its timer after a restart, as indicated by the documentation.\n\n\n`@monitor resume` is the first action to resume the timer. `@env-2` needs to finish the environment upgrade, including several feature updates and bug fixes, build the latest stage environment blend, and run preview checks before handing off to `@anim`. `@anim` needs to verify its edits and then run the final animation pipeline. Also, inform `@sfx` to re-run audio synthesis on the updated shots.\n\n\nInitial suspicion was a missed opportunity to ensure automatic resumption. Examining the documentation, a mechanism exists to awaken on `@coordinator` mentions. A brief must be created for each worker to post to `@coordinator` upon completion, ensuring the correct handoff chain. Verifying that the handoff sequence from `@env-2` to `@anim` to `@sfx` to `@verifier` to `@coordinator` is unbroken to ensure proper handoff and that resumption is triggered.\n\n\nIncorporating fixes from recent tasks, including track distance, radius adjustments, albedo correction, dedicated materials, sky dome smoothing, braking effects, shader updates, and clean collections. Then, the latest stage environment build must be verified through Python PIL metrics, ensuring proper handling of image files. Finally, the process posts handoff naming to `@anim`.\n\nAfter the server restart, verify upgraded animation scripts and incorporate fixes. If the environment build is not ready, the process will wait for the handoff from the environment agent. Once the stage environment blend is available, the build process can continue.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"post_message","args":{"text":"\"@monitor resume\""}},{"name":"post_message","args":{"text":"\"@env-2 Server restarted mid-turn — resume from where you left off (`pipeline/gen_textures.py` is already saved). Finish upgrading `pipeline/v5_env.py` incorporating all findings in #9 and #10 (`V5_Hangar` min track dist >= 180m, `V5_HedgeRing` radius >= 1500m, `V5_Stand_Complex` moved back `dist >= 38` so rail clears Copse track, `V5_Flag` `/255.0` linear albedo fix, dedicated single-user `Mat_FIA_RainLight`, smooth `V5_SkyDome` gradient, braking-zone skidmarks/DRS boards/pit timing, car paint/carbon/brake-rotor material polish, zero stranded root objects), run `v5_env.py` -> `LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend` and `v5_preview.py`, verify via Python PIL metrics (remember #7: NEVER call `read_file` on binary/image files), and post handoff naming `@anim`.\""}},{"name":"post_message","args":{"text":"\"@anim Server restarted mid-turn — resume from where you left off (`v5_anim.py`, `v5_clay.py`, `v5_stills.py`, `v5_viewport_fast.py` edits are on disk). Remember #7 (NEVER call `read_file` on binary/image files; use Python PIL/numpy + Blender headless checks). Check #11 from `sfx` for the exact audio/mux commands & metrics to include in `README.md`, `LATEST/README.txt`, and `docs/README_V5.md`. Wait via `swarm_wait` if `@env-2` hasn't finished `LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend` yet; as soon as `@env-2` hands off, run final `v5_anim.py` -> `LATEST/v5_stage_anim.blend`, `v5_clay.py` -> `LATEST/v5_stage_anim_clay.blend`, `v5_viewport_fast.py` fast/normal check, render all 26 1080p color stills + contact sheet (`renders_v5/stills/`) and clay test stills (`renders_v5/clay_stills/clay_test_*.jpg`), complete the docs sync, and post handoff naming `@sfx` (so `@sfx` refreshes `synth_sfx.py` + `--sfx-only` remux on your updated `SHOTS` camera positions and hands off to `@verifier`).\""}}]}
